Description: GtkGLArea: a size of their own for the views of a stereo area
 The views of a stereo area were rendered at the size of the area in device
 pixels, so a picture with a size of its own (a film) was resized twice: once
 by the program into the area's views, once by the compositor to the output.
 gtk_gl_area_set_stereo_view_size() sets the size one view is rendered at
 (properties stereo-view-width and stereo-view-height, -1 for the area's own
 size, the default). The picture handed to the compositor is then twice that
 width, and the compositor does the one resize to where the area is shown
 (wp_viewport on Wayland, _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_ONE_VIEW_SIZE on X11).
 The viewport is set to the view's size before each emission of the render
 signal for an area that asks for stereo, so a handler reads the size from the
 viewport whether the area is shown per eye or its left view alone at the
 area's size. An area that does not set a size, and every area without stereo,
 is as before.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (queue row 137, milestone 3)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
